    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0026" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.6359 International Nickel Company/28:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-13T13:00:00+02:00">March 13, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. My telegram No. 55, February 25.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d20-f1"/> Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs informed me today that Fieandt Delegation and Finnish Minister
                    there have returned from Moscow negotiations regarding deliveries from Russia
                    under trade agreement and regarding Petsamo nickel question being still in
                    suspense. He said Russians were taking position that pending acceptance by
                    Finnish Government of Soviet control of Chinese [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Petsamo</hi>] mines, deliveries under trade agreement would not be
                    forthcoming. Paasikivi will continue conversations with Molotov upon his return
                    to Moscow shortly. Witting did not seem especially concerned, however,
                    intimating that Russians remain preoccupied with developments in other areas
                    than Finland. He indicated also that Finnish Government is not now disposed to
                    change its position regarding control of nickel mines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
